Subject: i2c: designware: add snps,no-enable-abort / snps,no-sda-rx-hold opt-outs

Tree: /mnt/2tb/unvr-port-refs/linux-v7.3-fresh (torvalds/linux mainline)
Issue: #86, docs/rtc-s35390a-fault.md

Two per-controller DT opt-outs for mainline DesignWare i2c behaviour that
wedges the UNVR's pld bus:

- snps,no-enable-abort - __i2c_dw_disable() issuing IC_ENABLE.ABORT
  (mainline 2409205acd3c, 2023) terminates the transfer mid-byte. The
  S-35390A RTC (datasheet Fig 46) answers by holding SDA low until it is
  clocked through; the bus wedges and only a COLD power cycle recovers it.
  The vendor 4.19 kernel has no abort and does not wedge.
- snps,no-sda-rx-hold - suppresses the unconditional 1-tick RX SDA hold
  added alongside the TX hold. Not currently set by our DTS; kept with the
  abort opt-out because both are the same "do what the vendor driver did"
  escape hatch on the same controller.

Only snps,no-enable-abort is consumed by
dts/alpine-v2-ubnt-unvr-ea16.dts today. Both kernel build scripts FATAL if
the tree they are about to build does not honour it.

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
index a1eca6cd4b75..a4672c146943 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-common.c
@@ -599,7 +599,8 @@ static int i2c_dw_set_sda_hold(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
 		 * extends incoming SDA low to high transition while SCL is
 		 * high but it appears to help also above issue.
 		 */
-		if (!(dev->sda_hold_time & DW_IC_SDA_HOLD_RX_MASK))
+		if (!(dev->sda_hold_time & DW_IC_SDA_HOLD_RX_MASK) &&
+		    !device_property_read_bool(dev->dev, "snps,no-sda-rx-hold"))
 			dev->sda_hold_time |= 1 << DW_IC_SDA_HOLD_RX_SHIFT;
 
 		dev_dbg(dev->dev, "SDA Hold Time TX:RX = %d:%d\n",
@@ -643,6 +644,16 @@ void __i2c_dw_disable(struct dw_i2c_dev *dev)
 	if (dev->mode == DW_IC_SLAVE && (ic_stats & DW_IC_STATUS_SLAVE_ACTIVITY))
 		abort_needed = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * IC_ENABLE.ABORT terminates the transfer mid-byte, which some targets
+	 * (S-35390A, Fig 46) answer by holding SDA low until clocked through -
+	 * an unrecoverable bus wedge. Introduced in 2023 (2409205acd3c); the
+	 * vendor 4.19 kernel that drives this board has no abort and does not
+	 * wedge. Opt out per-controller.
+	 */
+	if (device_property_read_bool(dev->dev, "snps,no-enable-abort"))
+		abort_needed = false;
+
 	if (abort_needed) {
 		if (!(enable & DW_IC_ENABLE_ENABLE)) {
 			regmap_write(dev->map, DW_IC_ENABLE, DW_IC_ENABLE_ENABLE);
